Z||000006||ThatRickGuy||06-01-2000||12:24 PM||||I don't care for the "rice burneres" much myself either. But, I do respect them, I mean, sure they have no torque, and sound like "Pip farting on a snare drum". But they turn some high RPMs and get some good speed. As for the outrageous tires, well, their illegal in certain parts of the US (Try driving threw chicago w/ them!) for good reason! And the lowering thing, I can see wanting to be different and lower some interesting cars, but it just gets pointless. I saw a late 80's Suburban sitting 2 inches off the ground a few weeks ago, that just blew my mind. I am planing on lowering my fiero, with the 1 inch drop spring, but not to get the "low look" but for the handling reasons. And as for the exhaust, yeah, a high flow cat and super trap muffler would be nice, but there's nothing like the sound of a true Pontiac 450 running dual 2 1/2 inch exhaust w/ a wild cam. Torque and handling are where it's at for the street, high rev'rs are going to need a lower rear gear and will be less efficient and harder to drive, yeah, that calculated 200mph top end is nice, but it's not like you can &lt;legally&gt; do that anywheres but on a track. Ahh well, if they want to do it tho, it's their call, but if you wind up getting burned by a 4600 lbs old pontiac, just except in the power of torque.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
