Z||000010||stimpy||06-01-2000||07:37 PM||||Yeah, ok, hypocrite here. whatever. <BR>Bam, having grown up in East Side San Jose, the birthplace of the modern lowrider movement, yeah, I have a pretty square idea of what a cholo is. And I understand that it is not neccesarily (sp?) a derogetory word. But a cholo car? I don't know. I guess I am just getting a little bored with the "us vs them" vibe. I think it is GREAT that homie gets a lump in his throat when he looks at his Fiero, but why turn it in to a slam on other people in general. I have shaken my head and snickered at certain examples of poor taste. But there are fine examples of Japanese engineering, and yes, styling. I really do like lowriders, altough I'd never juice my GT and give it a velour and mirror interior, I would like to build a clean lowrider Cutlass someday.  <BR>I guess what I am trying to say is that any one of "us" could be "them".<BR>Why not focus on the positives that make "us" us and not get into the trap of making fun of "them".<BR>Besides that, y'all should know by know that I am a grumpy pisser in the morning. If you see an early time on my post, take it with a grain of salt.<P>And Bam, lets not go there, OK? ||||reg||1
